# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# test/deploy.test.js asserts an agent body matches /^---\n/ — front-matter
# detection. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a checkout rewrites
# that to `---\r\n` and the assertion fails, so the suite passes on Linux CI and
# fails on every Windows machine. Upstream has no .gitattributes, which is why
# that test is red on Windows and green in CI.
#
# Force LF in the working tree, everywhere, so the tests mean the same thing on
# every platform. `git add --renormalize .` after changing this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
